---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
---

<Layout title="About — LFNW Trip" description="About this LinuxFest Northwest trip planner.">
  <Nav />
  <main>
    <div class="about-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="section-label">About This Site</p>
        <h1>LinuxFest Northwest 2027</h1>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="container">
      <div class="about-grid">
        <section class="card about-card">
          <h2>The Trip</h2>
          <p>
            A solo road trip to Bellingham, Washington for <a href="https://www.linuxfestnorthwest.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinuxFest Northwest</a>.
          </p>
          <ul class="about-list">
            <li>🚗 Driving from Seattle (~90 miles each way via I-5)</li>
            <li>📅 April 23–25, 2027 (3 days)</li>
            <li>🐧 LinuxFest Northwest: Apr 23–25</li>
            <li>🌲 Solo traveler</li>
            <li>🍦 Ice cream selfie tradition (4 spots planned)</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="card about-card">
          <h2>The Site</h2>
          <p>
            This is a personal trip planner built with <a href="https://astro.build" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Astro</a>
            and hosted on <a href="https://pages.github.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub Pages</a>.
            It's part of a monorepo of trip planners at <a href="/" >sfalken.github.io</a>.
          </p>
          <ul class="about-list">
            <li>🗺️ Interactive maps (Leaflet + OpenStreetMap)</li>
            <li>✅ Planning checklist with browser persistence</li>
            <li>💰 Budget tracker with expense logging</li>
            <li>📱 Progressive Web App (installable, offline-capable)</li>
            <li>🔒 Optional PII encryption for booking details</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="card about-card">
          <h2>LinuxFest Northwest</h2>
          <p>
            LFNW is a free-to-attend, community-run open source and Linux conference hosted at Bellingham Technical College
            since 2000, co-produced with Jupiter Broadcasting.
          </p>
          <p style="margin-top:.75rem;">
            The call for speakers is open from Oct 12, 2026 to Jan 15, 2027. Speakers are unpaid. The schedule and
            attendee registration details had not been published when this site was built.
          </p>
          <a href="https://www.linuxfestnorthwest.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-primary" style="margin-top:1rem;align-self:flex-start;">
            Visit linuxfestnorthwest.org →
          </a>
        </section>

        <section class="card about-card">
          <h2>Bellingham, Washington</h2>
          <p>
            Bellingham sits on Bellingham Bay near the Canadian border, about 90 miles north of Seattle. It has a
            walkable downtown, the historic Fairhaven district, and a strong craft beer and ice cream scene.
          </p>
          <ul class="about-list">
            <li>🕐 Timezone: Pacific Time (same as Seattle)</li>
            <li>🚗 Drive: I-5 north, roughly 2 hours each way</li>
            <li>🌧️ April: cool and often showery — pack a rain jacket</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .about-hero {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--wa-primary) 0%, var(--wa-accent) 100%);
    color: white;
    padding: 2.5rem 0 2rem;
  }
  .about-hero .section-label { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.7); }
  .about-hero h1 { color: white; }

  .about-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(300px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .about-card {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }
  .about-card h2 { font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--wa-primary); }
  .about-card p { font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--gray-700); line-height: 1.6; }

  .about-list {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--gray-700);
  }
</style>
